## Container and image identity

Local images use a commit-derived tag by default:

```bash
make docker-build
```

CI never publishes `:latest`. A push to `main` publishes:

```text
ghcr.io/{{ github_owner }}/{{ project_name }}:<full-git-sha>
```

The publish job requests BuildKit SBOM and max-level provenance attestations. It then uses the exact build output digest to retrieve the registry-attached SPDX SBOM and fails closed unless that payload is a valid SPDX document with creation metadata and a non-empty package inventory. Only after that check does the job sign the immutable image digest with keyless Cosign using GitHub OIDC.

## CI behavior

Pull requests run formatting, vet, lint, race-enabled tests, filesystem/dependency vulnerability scanning, and a container build without publishing.

`main` runs the same quality/security gates, then authenticates to GHCR with `GITHUB_TOKEN`, publishes a full-SHA image, verifies the SBOM attached to the exact published digest, and signs that digest.

## Observability

The template provides structured JSON request logs and Prometheus metrics. Distributed tracing is an explicit extension point rather than a pretend default: add OpenTelemetry instrumentation/exporters when the service has a trace backend and propagate context across outbound dependencies.

## GitOps onboarding

Application deployment state belongs in the Golden Path GitOps repository, not in this application repository. The expected service path is:

```text
gitops-config/apps/team-{{ team }}/{{ project_name }}/
```

Reference the immutable image produced by this repository and promote the same artifact through dev -> staging -> prod. Do not rebuild per environment.

